## Architecture

**Ports-and-adapters** (hexagonal): the domain sits in the centre and depends on nothing outside itself. Outer layers (`{{ package_name }}.cli`) import the domain, never the reverse. import-linter enforces this (`uv run poe imports`, contract in `importlinter.ini`) — when you add a package, add it to the layers contract.

For services or modules with real domain logic, follow the `cosmic-python` skill (`.claude/skills/cosmic-python/SKILL.md`): domain model, repository, service layer, unit of work, events. Keep simple scripts simple.

## Layout

    src/{{ package_name }}/domain/   # pure logic, no I/O, no outward imports
    src/{{ package_name }}/cli/      # entry points driving the domain
    tests/                         # pytest; mirrors src/ structure
    scripts/                       # dev tooling (complexity gate, hook installer)
